comment.narrative:
The direct beneficiaries of the e-Gabon project are patients, national health system workers, as well as private sector actors and entrepreneurs, with a particular focus on women and young people seeking to do business in the digital economy. As a result, the direct beneficiaries of the project are as follows:
4,859 SIS workers (including 3,687 women);
872 hackathon participants (including 178 women);
1,625 participants in training courses offered by incubators (including 719 women);
450 beneficiaries identified in 2018

